FILE: app/src/watched-manager.ts
```ts
import {
    createAnimationManager,
    createAnimationTask,
    addAnimationTask,
    type AnimationManager,
} from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function createWatchedManager(onStep: (stepMs: number) => void): AnimationManager {
    const manager = createAnimationManager();
    const task = createAnimationTask((mgr, deltaMs) => {
        const step = mgr.fixedDeltaMs > 0 ? mgr.fixedDeltaMs : deltaMs;
        onStep(step);
    });
    addAnimationTask(manager, task);
    return manager;
}
```

I created `src/watched-manager.ts`, which builds a plain manager and adds a single untitled task that fires `onStep` with the effective step (respecting `fixedDeltaMs` per note 20) on every `updateAnimationManager` call. I was not fully certain whether the `deltaMs` delivered to a task is the raw argument or already adjusted for `fixedDeltaMs`, but checking `manager.fixedDeltaMs` explicitly makes the code correct in either case.
